course: dictionary
lesson: 13572
title: Inauspicious beginnings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word inauspicious has a small hidden clue. The in- at the start means not, and an inauspicious thing is one that does not look lucky or promising. «The bus broke down before it left the station, an inauspicious start to our trip.» The bus breaking down is a bad sign, so inauspicious must mean showing that things will go badly.
explain: Look at the words around it. Start and trip tell you this is about a beginning and a journey. Broke down tells you something went wrong. Put your meaning in the sentence: «an unlucky start to our trip» still makes sense, so you have worked it out.
explain: Inauspicious is a formal word, so you will meet it mostly in stories, news and history. Writers use it to warn the reader. «The sky turned black and a crow sat on the roof, an inauspicious sign» tells you that trouble may be coming, even before anything has happened.
fact: Inauspicious means showing signs that things will go badly; unlucky or not a good start.
fact: «An inauspicious start» means a bad beginning, though things may still get better later.
fact: Writers use inauspicious to hint that trouble is coming.
fact: Long ago, some people believed in omens, so they thought certain days or signs were inauspicious.
fact: Inauspicious is formal, so it is most often found in stories, news and history books.
exercise: «The bus broke down before it left the station, an inauspicious start to our trip.» What does inauspicious mean here? | Quick and easy | Lucky and full of promise | *Showing signs that things will go badly | Very loud
exercise: Which of these is an inauspicious start? | Everyone arrived early and smiling | *The bike got a flat tyre on the very first mile | The sun came out and the band began to play | The cake was warm and sweet
exercise: Why might a writer use «inauspicious» in a story? | To make the reader fall asleep | To show that the party is about to begin | To describe a happy dog | *To hint that trouble is coming
test: «The match began with a red card and a broken goal post, an inauspicious start.» What does inauspicious mean? | *Unlucky, showing that things may go badly | Sunny and warm | Exciting and full of goals | Very short
test: Ruby says an inauspicious start is a great beginning. What is wrong with her idea? | It means the start was too loud | It means the opposite: a beginning that looks like things will go badly | *Nothing is wrong, it means a great beginning | It means the start was too late
exam: In the story, «the cracked mirror fell from the wall on the day the family moved in, an inauspicious beginning». What does inauspicious mean, and what clue in the sentence helps you know? | Lucky, because the family moved in | *Showing that things will go badly, because the mirror cracked and fell | Long and tiring, because they moved far | Quiet, because the mirror was on the wall
